    "result_text": "The build passes. The single test class (`AcceptanceTest`, the new `displayName` acceptance test) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created, the API now returns a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema (and to its `required` list). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the fetch responder (`RespondWithOwner`) go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the computed `displayName` is present on both the POST result and subsequent GETs, derived from the persisted `lastName`/`firstName`.",
